  m_Name: NestedCage
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GravityBox.Gameplay::GravityBox.Gameplay.LevelDefinition
  Id: steel-lab-nestedcage
  DisplayIndex: 19
  DisplayName: A box within a box
  Shape: 18
  TeachingHint: The inner cage hangs under gravity. Tilt past its stop to line up
    the mouth.
  Environment: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 82e0ce24addfe4fc89b8bbd0db998aea, type: 2}
  Prefab: {fileID: 8264946853585964152, guid: 03b890ae554e74c65ab2f971e15ba6b8, type: 3}
  RotationMode: 1
  InitialLocalVelocity: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  ParSeconds: 0
  Tutorial: 0
  DesignerSolution: The counterweighted inner cage rotates independently on its bearing.
    Tilt the outer enclosure past the visible bearing stop so the inner floor slopes
    towards its only mouth. Transfer the ball onto the outer landing tray, then guide
    it to the round exit. The cage is a real compound dynamic body. Shared exit assist
    pulls the ball through an unobstructed opening within 40 mm. This is deliberate
    gameplay assistance; the entire sphere must still physically clear the bore before
    completion.
